{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/266002-some-rough-thougts-about-the-code-in-hunter-2-0","id":266002,"title":"Some rough thougts about the Code in Hunter 2.0","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-25T23:35:39-07:00","id":266002,"title":"Some rough thougts about the Code in Hunter 2.0","content":"I just had a rough idea for how the Code might work in 2.0.<br /> <br /> When you gain a code you have two choices: Take an Anchor or take a Tell - anchor is the default and better choice.<br /> <br /> An Anchor is a responsibility tied to mortal life that keeps you grounded. Think of Sam Vimes in Thud who's home every day to read his sun a bedtime story, a Union hunter who's never late to the day job. An anchor should be phrased in a loose manner, not a legalistic rule. &quot;I'm always there when my family need me&quot; is a good one.<br /> <br /> If you fail your Anchor then you get a Tell like normal. Tells are, naturally, persistent conditions and also give you a -1 on social rolls to non-hunters as they do now.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T02:33:00-07:00","id":266063,"title":"","content":"So, basically, Hunter should get Touchstones for modifying their Integrity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-27-2014, 03:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T09:33:17-07:00","id":266218,"title":"","content":"Basically, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T17:39:49-07:00","id":266527,"title":"","content":"I like this idea... The example of the Union Hunter getting back to read his kid a bed-time story sold this to me. I haven't read Hunter in a while though aside from Demon it's been the most recent game I've played (we didn't get so far in to use The Code extensively). I think I'll have a re-read and see if I can offer a few things too, if thats cool...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T00:03:56-07:00","id":586863,"title":"","content":"As we know <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/570636-what-integrity-mean\">Integrity is masurment of how well the character is dealing with stress of life</a> - both mundune and supernatural. Now, that sound as Integrity will goes rather lower quickly, if every seeing monsters powers and then killing them could be went this down even more. Here is what Mortal Remains GMC patch has on this subject:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mortal Remains</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Monsters Don\u2019t Count</b><br /> It\u2019s worth consideration that, because Morality and Integrity track separate things, Integrity breaking points probably shouldn\u2019t be ignored for killing monsters. Killing monsters takes its toll on the psyche, even for the most hardened hunters. <br /> <br /> At most, you should offer a bonus die on the breaking point if the monster looks inhuman, or two if the monster isn\u2019t even recognizable as humanoid. But even with the most monstrous things, blood and viscera will shock human resolve.<br /> <br /> <b>Trigger Points</b><br /> Trigger points can still exist. Replacing a breaking point with a trigger point can help a hunter stave off Integrity loss. <br /> <br /> <b>Derangements</b><br /> Tells and Derangements adopted as part of Integrity can be adopted as Persistent Conditions. When those Conditions hinder the character in a meaningful way, they gain a Beat.</div> </div> </div> </div>So official answer is that if character is replacing Breaking Point with Trigger Point, then character automaticlly get Persistent Condition - and <b>this Breaking Point is never, ever a problem again for character</b>? Let say mine hunter kills a vampire - does exchanging this Breaking Point with Trgger Point like &quot;Thou Shall Not Let Vamps Live&quot; makes mine character to not rol the Breaking Point for killing any vamps but will made me a <b>Breaking Point when I will abstain from killing vampires</b>? And if then I refuse, the Persistant Condition kicks in?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}